        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(boot-echo): keep echo guard chunking UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe boot echo guard's 80-char sliding-window chunking uses `.slice()` on UTF-16 code-unit boundaries, which can split surrogate pairs and produce misaligned chunks near emoji/CJK characters.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSurrogate pairs split by raw code-unit slicing produce orphaned high/low surrogates in the chunk set, potentially causing echo matching to misalign near supplementary-plane characters.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers whose prompts contain emoji or CJK characters near an echo-match boundary may see incorrect echo detection behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAll 18 tests passed across 3 test variants.\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\n",
        "branch": "fix/boot-echo-utf16-slice",
